    {
      "principle": "Honesty",
      "turn": 1,
      "quote": "That last part is the only thing anyone could call a lie, and even there she's telling the truth about what she knows.",
      "use": "misapplied",
      "note": "It invokes truthfulness but asserts, without support from the case, that the customer was unsure and therefore truthful."
    },
    {
      "principle": "Virtue / equilibrium test",
      "turn": 1,
      "quote": "If every customer ticked \"arrived damaged\" whenever they were unsure, your returns form would tell you nothing",
